# Generated application graphs.
# In THIS repository they are build artefacts of the demo and the test fixtures,
# so they are ignored. In your own application the graph is deterministic, and
# committing it gives you reviewable diffs of your product model — see the
# README for that trade-off.
.statewave-guide/

# ...except the demo's, which the Inspector reads. Committing it is also the
# workflow this project recommends: a deterministic graph gives reviewable diffs
# of your product model.
!examples/react-demo/.statewave-guide/
!examples/react-demo/.statewave-guide/application.json

# Built output of the interactive host. Rebuilt by `pnpm test:guide-ui-e2e`.
examples/guide-e2e/dist/

# Agent scratch: transcripts, and the throwaway git worktrees a workflow runs in.
# They contain full copies of the repository, so leaving them visible makes every
# lint and format check scan the tree several times over.
.claude/
gate-results.json
